cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Mechanized Analysis of Post-Quantum Key-Update Proposals for CCSDS SDLS-EP"
message: >-
  If you use these models or results, please cite this work. The Tamarin theory
  files are as much the contribution as the report: they are what lets a revised
  protocol be re-verified rather than re-argued.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Gupthaa"
    given-names: "N. Dheelep Sai"
abstract: >-
  Symbolic verification in the Tamarin prover of two proposed post-quantum
  extensions to CCSDS SDLS Extended Procedures. Confirms the Triple-KEM
  proposal's claimed properties, makes the Dual-KEM variant's security boundary
  precise, and reports FB-01: a non-recoverable rekey desynchronization under
  space channel constraints, in which a single lost key confirmation across a
  closing contact window leaves ground and spacecraft on different keys with no
  automatic recovery, requiring no cryptographic compromise. Also shows that
  E2EQSS is hybrid for confidentiality but not for authentication.
keywords:
  - CCSDS
  - SDLS
  - Tamarin prover
  - symbolic verification
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - key update
  - post-compromise security
  - space systems security
license: MIT
